Apple has made one thing very clear it  will not put touch screens on Macs but  that doesn't mean others can't try this  is the neo node air bar and it claims to  turn any MacBook Air screen into a  touchscreen I can come to CES 2017  without trying it clip the magnetic air  bar to the bottom bezel plug it into the  USB port and boom you can control the  screen with your fingers  it doesn't actually create a touchscreen  though according to a senior vice  president at neo node it creates an  invisible light above the screen so when  the user touches the screen the sensor  realizes the touch event of course it  does just tap out an application icon  and it launches no special software  required you can swipe through photos  pan around maps rearrange icons into  folders and yes write and draw right on  the screen you can even add those  beautiful finishing touches to your  presentation and worried about closing  your laptop on the air bar don't worry  this happens if you try I was shocked at  how well it worked but it isn't perfect  especially when you consider that Mac OS  was designed for a mouse sometimes it's  a bit jumpy and it isn't even worth  trying to hit small targets on the  screen you can't scroll on webpages or  pinch to zoom though the company says  it's planning to add that soon plus it  only works with the 13-inch MacBook Air  the air bar will be out in March for $99  it's pretty cool maybe it'll even  convince those guys in Cupertino to  rethink that whole no touch screen on  Mac rule  you
 

